\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Scalar, Pareto, and robust frontiers}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{multi-objective}

\p{For a fixed FTIP instance, the \strong{attainable set} contains the pairs
of evaluation outcomes and lifecycle costs produced by trusted protocols. A
\strong{scalar frontier} orders outcomes with one utility. A \strong{Pareto
frontier} retains outcomes that cannot improve one coordinate without
worsening another. A \strong{robust value} takes the minimum outcome over a
declared family of evaluation groups.}

\p{Pareto order is a standard construction in multi-objective optimization.
Worst-group utility is a standard robust objective. Their application to the FTIP
attainable set is an FTIP synthesis. They are grouped here because they are
alternative orderings of the same feasible set.}

\p{The choice cannot be hidden inside notation. A scalar average may conceal
a subgroup loss, while a worst-group objective may sacrifice total utility.
The theorem statement must name the ordering it uses.}
